  "scope": "Group-progress projection from the original memory journal or a single native SQLite read transaction: standalone/next/pending/completed selection, lazy plan/request/terminal decoding and ordered branch-token observations.",
  "limitations": [
    "Frozen pre-extraction projection bodies keep original SQL and decision order. Native storage, codecs, request/terminal admission and existing group evaluation remain shared; migrated selection policy is not shared.",
    "The 1680 memory cases cover 70 original operations, two execution orders and twelve low-level states, including absent rows, partial acknowledgement/terminal state, duplicate membership, first-owner selection and unvalidated memory payloads.",
    "The 192 SQLite cases cover four group forms, three lifecycle stages and sixteen low-level scenarios. Corrupt fixtures exercise original fault precedence and are not supported recovery checkpoints; production schema constraints are unchanged.",
    "Twelve memory and twelve durable complete shapes use public claim/acknowledgement through tail, capture, multiple capture and conditional groups. Durable final observations survive reopen without changing their result.",
    "The two-connection snapshot test enables WAL after opening both test connections, commits a real branch acknowledgement after the first progress query, and verifies request/prefix reads remain on the previous snapshot. A new read sees the new commit. Production keeps DELETE journal mode.",
    "Memory and durable projection intentionally retain different admission and successor-marker checks. Durable count conversion precedes state checks; only a last-pending parallel group probes its plan. Unknown order handling is unchanged, not newly admitted recovery authority.",
    "Native owners retain transaction lifetime and all SQL diagnostics. The adapter introduces no writes, retries, cache publication, ID allocation or independent commit.",
    "No new Linux, remote CI, live GUI, actual exported-source execution, full host-neutral durable recovery, power-loss, disk-full, multi-host race or throughput evidence is claimed."
  ],
